  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "As we know compound (d) is aromatic and the compound (a) is anti-aromatic. Hence compound (d) is most stable and compound (a) is least stable among these in compound (b) and (c) carbon atom of that positive charge is $\\mathrm{sp}^3$ hybridised they on the basis of angle strain theory compound (c) is more stable than compound (b).\n<img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/6b3DV3CpFQU7gTtCp99ww3hFbDoUJUp5-Y_l2lbxNps.original.fullsize.png\"><br>",
